From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aayush Nair <aayushnair204@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 01:36:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Documentation: kernel-parameters: Describe kairos.noscheduler

The word keeps the kernel from attaching Kairos Scheduler before init
(CONFIG_KAIROS_BOOT_SCHEDULER), and Kairos's init reads it too.

Signed-off-by: Aayush Nair <aayushnair204@gmail.com>
---
 Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt b/Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt
index 03a550630644f43d36b69ae79e6d66f42d75426d..9c163139a158fdb5274b164aa6bfa053d8d85d43 100644
--- a/Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt
+++ b/Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt
@@ -2900,6 +2900,11 @@ Kernel parameters
 	js=		[HW,JOY] Analog joystick
 			See Documentation/input/joydev/joystick.rst.
 
+	kairos.noscheduler
+			[KNL] Don't attach Kairos Scheduler before init
+			(CONFIG_KAIROS_BOOT_SCHEDULER). Kairos's init reads
+			the same word and leaves the scheduler off too.
+
 	kasan_multi_shot
 			[KNL] Enforce KASAN (Kernel Address Sanitizer) to print
 			report on every invalid memory access. Without this
